# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rich Friends — environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local: leave DATABASE_URL empty → JSON files under .data/
# Production (Vercel + Supabase): set DATABASE_URL to the Supabase connection
# string (Project Settings → Database → Connection string → URI).
#
# Prefer the "Transaction" pooler URI (port 6543) on Vercel serverless:
#   postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[PASSWORD]@aws-0-[REGION].pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
#
# Or the direct connection (port 5432) for migrations / long-lived processes:
#   postgresql://postgres:[PASSWORD]@db.[PROJECT-REF].supabase.co:5432/postgres
#
# If you link Supabase ↔ Vercel, the integration often injects POSTGRES_URL
# (and related keys). This app accepts DATABASE_URL or POSTGRES_URL.
#
# After creating the project, run supabase/schema.sql once in the Supabase SQL Editor.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=
# POSTGRES_URL=   # optional; set automatically by the Supabase Vercel integration
